  "packageSize": 2561934,
  "published": "2026-11-23T17:01:01.407Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "## Changes since 0.3.0\n\n### Added\n- `show` reports per-version deprecation. Text output gains a trailing `Deprecation=[reasons]` segment with the server's reason words verbatim, and `Deprecation=unspecified` when the server gives none. A deprecated version with a custom message prints one stderr hint to rerun with `--output json` for the full record.\n- `show --output json` lines gain a fourth `deprecation` field holding the full record, or JSON `null` when not deprecated. This changes the documented three-field `show` NDJSON schema; `unlist` is unchanged.\n\n### Changed\n- The `sdk` backend passes the API key to `dotnet nuget delete` via the child process's `NUGET_API_KEY` environment variable instead of the command line, so it no longer shows up in process listings.\n- `--unlist-all` treats stable `0.x` versions as pre-release, so packages published only as `0.x` are no longer skipped.\n- Dependency Updates: NuGet.Protocol 8.0.0, Microsoft.Extensions.* 11.0.0, System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs 11.0.0, CliInvoke 3.2.0-beta.1, DotMake.CommandLine 3.8.0, Polyfill 12.0.0, TUnit 1.84.0, FsCheck 3.6.0, plus workflow action bumps.\n\n### Removed\n- `--include-zero-major`, now part of the pre-release definition itself.\n\n### Fixed\n- `show` observes Ctrl-C during the deprecation pass and exits `130`.\n- Feed-side read failures print a one-line diagnostic naming the package id and server URL instead of a stack trace.",
